body:
@MarianoGnu You were completely right about the runtime behavior, but the fix actually needed to happen in the static analyzer! I updated gdscript_analyzer.cpp so that expressions using ?. now explicitly downgrade their inferred return type to Variant (since it can short-circuit to Nil).
Reference: 
<img width="1919" height="1031" alt="image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/af1d220c-423d-43fa-81d4-1c22ab89761c" />

As you can see, assigning a ?. result to a strict int now correctly throws the expected runtime type error (Trying to assign value of type 'Nil' to a variable of type 'int'). The weird, silent conversion you spotted should be gone now.

@HolonProduction I understand what you're implying and thanks for pointing it out (I wasn't honestly aware of such a language feature). I'll look into it soon enough (sorry for the inconvience but a human such as me needs to rest too 😓), but I'll definitely take the advice and try to implement the ?? operator next so they can be pushed together. Thanks for the feedback!
